    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "1TH",
      "chapter": 5,
      "chapter_usfm": "1TH.5",
      "version_id": 90,
      "version_abbr": "LEB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now concerning the times and the seasons, brothers, you have no need of anything to be written to you,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "for you yourselves well know that the day of the Lord is coming in the same way as a thief in the night."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Whenever they say “Peace and security,” then sudden destruction will overtake them like the birth pains of a pregnant woman, and they will not possibly escape."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But you, brothers, are not in the darkness, so that the day should catch you like a thief,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "for you are all sons of light and sons of day. We are not of the night nor of darkness."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So then, we must not sleep like the rest, but must be on the alert and be self-controlled."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For those who sleep, sleep at night, and those who get drunk, are drunk at night."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But because we are of the day, we must be sober, by putting on the breastplate of faith and love and as a helmet the hope of salvation,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "because God did not appoint us for wrath, but for the obtaining of salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "who died for us, so that whether we are awake or asleep, we will live at the same time with him."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore encourage one another and build up each other, just as indeed you are doing."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now we ask you, brothers, to respect those who labor among you and rule over you in the Lord and admonish you,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and to esteem them beyond all measure in love, because of their work. Be at peace among yourselves."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And we urge you, brothers, admonish the disorderly, console the discouraged, help the sick, be patient toward all people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "See to it that no one pays back evil for evil to anyone, but always pursue good toward one another and toward all people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Rejoice always,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "pray constantly,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "give thanks in everything; for this is the will of God for you in Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Do not quench the Spirit."
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Do not despise prophecies,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "but examine all things; hold fast to what is good."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Abstain from every form of evil."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now may the God of peace himself sanctify you completely, and may your spirit and soul and body be kept complete, blameless at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The one who calls you is faithful, who also will do this."
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Brothers, pray for us."
        },
        {
          "verse": 26,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.26",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss."
        },
        {
          "verse": 27,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.27",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I adjure you by the Lord, have this letter read aloud to all the brothers."
        },
        {
          "verse": 28,
          "usfm": "1TH.5.28",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 28,
      "headings": [
        {
          "before_verse": 12,
          "text": "Final Exhortations and Benediction"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
